      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Liver hemangiomas are the most common benign liver mass and typically asymptomatic and incidentally found. Giant liver hemangiomas are defined as having an overall diameter of >5 cm and more likely to be symptomatic. We present a case of a dominant caudate lobe hemangioma presented with weight loss and abdominal pain."},
